<!--
The chrome every blog post wears, nested INSIDE the site `Layout`: the site
shell is already applied by the router's declaration, so this file adds only
what an article has and a docs page does not, and never repeats the document
(no <html>, no <head>, no header or footer).

Nesting is by ancestry, so the wrapping is `Layout(ArticleLayout(post))`:
declared on <Route path="blog"> in main.bsx, it reaches every discovered post
and nothing else.

<ArticleHeader/> renders the title, byline and video embed from the post's own
frontmatter, so a post is its prose and nothing else. It renders nothing for a
page with no `created` date, which is what lets the undated blog index share
this layout and keep its own heading.

The comments are the replies to the post's announcement on Bluesky, read live
from the AppView, so they sit in a server island behind a minute's edge cache:
the page itself stays cached for the week. Its fallback, shown until the island
swaps in and for good with scripts off, is the link to reply on Bluesky. A post
with no announcement renders neither.
-->
<ArticleHeader/>
<slot/>
<ServerIsland name="comments" {CacheHeaders{edge_max_age: "60s"}}>
	<StandardSiteComments/>
	<StandardSiteReplyLink slot="fallback"/>
</ServerIsland>
